Build native CUDA code for Maxwell through Volta, and let those cards
past the compute-capability gate. Opt-in: build_physx.py applies this
only under --legacy-gpu, and reverse-applies it on any run without the
flag, so the default build is unchanged.

The reduced SASS list (after patch 0002) is 75,80,86,89,90,100,120, and
CMake separately injects compute_52, so the shipped PhysXGpu_64.dll
carries cubins and PTX for eight architectures: sm_52 and sm_75 through
sm_120. CudaContextManager.cpp then refuses any device below compute
7.0. Maxwell, Pascal and the GTX 10-series are rejected outright, which
is the behaviour this patch exists to change.

Both halves have to move together, and not for the reason it looks
like. Lowering the floor alone does NOT leave a card with nothing to
run -- the compute_52 PTX image is forward-compatible, so the driver
JIT-compiles every PhysX kernel for a GTX 1080 at load and the card
works, several times slower than native, with no diagnostic that
distinguishes it from a native run. Worse, CudaContextManager.cpp:673
excludes CUDA_ERROR_NO_BINARY_FOR_GPU from its error path and
mIsValid is already true by then, so a missing cubin is reported as
nothing at all and the context advertises itself as healthy. A
half-applied change therefore ships a silently slow or silently
broken GPU path rather than a clean failure. Keeping both edits in one
-p1 diff makes "neither half alone" true by construction instead of by
convention.

Compute 5.0 is the one capability with genuinely nothing loadable: a
sm_52 cubin cannot run on a 5.0 device (cubins are forward-compatible
only within a major version) and compute_52 PTX cannot target it
either. Lowering the floor to 5 admits exactly that device, so the
sm_50 this patch adds is what keeps the lowered floor honest -- which
is the second reason the two edits cannot be separated.

Widen both the reduced and full SASS lists to
50,60,61,70,75,80,86,89,90,100,120, exactly as 0002 widened both, and
lower MIN_SM_MAJOR_VERSION from 7 to 5 (the minor stays 0). 70 is
included because Volta is compute 7.0 and already passes the gate
today, so it is JIT-compiling from compute_52 PTX in the default build
-- the same latent bug 0002 fixed for Turing. 61 is named alongside 60
because whether a sm_60 cubin covers a 6.1 device is unverified here.

Costs CUDA compile time and disk. 8 architectures become 12, and CUDA
is 86% of this build's compile work. Measured on 32 cores under CUDA
12.8, a full SDK build goes from 100.3 s to 172.5 s of ninja wall time
and from 36.7 to 72.0 CUDA cpu-minutes -- the architecture count rises
by half but the work very nearly doubles, because the four legacy
targets are no cheaper to compile than the modern ones. The DLL grows
from 346,803,712 to 501,424,640 bytes (331 MB to 478 MB), carrying 732
cubin sections instead of 488.

Needs CUDA 12.x. CUDA 13's nvcc dropped all four of sm_50/60/61/70 --
its floor is compute_75 and it fails with "nvcc fatal : Unsupported gpu
architecture", so it rejects this patch's arch list rather than quietly
omitting it. No runtime effect on compute 7.5 and newer, which keep
exactly the cubins they have today.

diff --git a/physx/source/compiler/cmakegpu/CMakeLists.txt b/physx/source/compiler/cmakegpu/CMakeLists.txt
index da02fbe..e5b932f 100644
--- a/physx/source/compiler/cmakegpu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/physx/source/compiler/cmakegpu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -94,10 +94,10 @@ SET(SOURCE_DISTRO_FILE_LIST "")
 # since that's the default set in: compiler\internal\CMakeLists.txt (using CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES)
 # see policy CMP0104
 IF(PX_GENERATE_GPU_REDUCED_ARCHITECTURES)
-	GENERATE_ARCH_CODE_LIST(SASS "75,80,86,89,90,100,120" PTX "120")
+	GENERATE_ARCH_CODE_LIST(SASS "50,60,61,70,75,80,86,89,90,100,120" PTX "120")
 ELSE()
 	# Volta is the minimum compute arch required because NGC supports V100
-	GENERATE_ARCH_CODE_LIST(SASS "70,75,80,86,89,90,100,120" PTX "120")
+	GENERATE_ARCH_CODE_LIST(SASS "50,60,61,70,75,80,86,89,90,100,120" PTX "120")
 ENDIF()
 
 # Force response files off because clangd does not parse them
diff --git a/physx/source/cudamanager/src/CudaContextManager.cpp b/physx/source/cudamanager/src/CudaContextManager.cpp
index dbd620d..03d17a1 100644
--- a/physx/source/cudamanager/src/CudaContextManager.cpp
+++ b/physx/source/cudamanager/src/CudaContextManager.cpp
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ namespace physx
 #define MIN_CUDA_VERSION			12000	// Use Cuda toolkit 12.0 and above
 #define NV_DRIVER_MAJOR_VERSION		527
 #define NV_DRIVER_MINOR_VERSION		41
-#define MIN_SM_MAJOR_VERSION		7
+#define MIN_SM_MAJOR_VERSION		5
 #define MIN_SM_MINOR_VERSION		0
 
 #define USE_DEFAULT_CUDA_STREAM		0
